<title>INDIA: Indian Hotels 1996/97 1st half net up.</title>
<headline>Indian Hotels 1996/97 1st half net up.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	 513.2    vs     442.6</p>
<p>    Net sales	2,396.3    vs   2,087.6</p>
<p>    Other income     109.6    vs	84.9</p>
<p>    Expenditure    1,572.7    vs   1,358.1</p>
<p>    Interest costs   195.8    vs     180.4</p>
<p>    Depreciation     104.2    vs	85.4</p>
<p>    Tax		  120.0    vs     106.0</p>
<p>Note: Indian Hotels Company is the flagship of the Taj group of hotels, the country's largest hospitality group</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom (91-22-265 9000)</p>
</text>
